UID:2027-01-26-run1-sharpener-4-x-2-min@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270126T063000
DTEND:20270126T070000
SUMMARY:[RW] Sharpener (4 x 2 min) (30 min)
DESCRIPTION:10 min warm-up\; 4 x (2 min threshold + 2 min easy)\; 8 min co
 ol-down. Short and crisp\, then stop. The taper keeps a little intensity 
 while volume drops (Bosquet 2007).\n\nWeek 10 (TAPER). Not medical advice
 \; pain that changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-27-bike1-sharpener-ride-4-x-2@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270127T063000
DTEND:20270127T072000
SUMMARY:[RW] Sharpener ride (4 x 2 min) (50 min)
DESCRIPTION:12 min warm-up\; 10 min easy\; 4 x (2 min threshold + 3 min ea
 sy)\; 8 min cool-down. Short and crisp\, then stop (taper: volume down\, 
 intensity kept).\n\nWeek 10 (TAPER). Not medical advice\; pain that chang
 es how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-30-activation-activation-20-min-ea@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270130T090000
DTEND:20270130T092000
SUMMARY:[RW] Activation (20 min easy run + 3 short pickups) (20 min)
DESCRIPTION:20 min easy with 3 pickups of 15 s at race effort. Pack your k
 it\, check your gear\, eat normally\, sleep.\n\nWeek 10 (TAPER). Not medi
 cal advice\; pain that changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2027-01-31-race-race-day-sprint-duat@rampwise
DTSTAMP:20261117T003912Z
DTSTART:20270131T080000
DTEND:20270131T090000
SUMMARY:[RW] RACE DAY: Sprint duathlon (run\, ride\, run)
DESCRIPTION:Run the first kilometre about 5 % slower than your planned pac
 e (Walsh 2019\, one elite study). Start easier than feels necessary for t
 he first third. Eat and drink as practised\, nothing new. It is a day to 
 enjoy the work you did\; no plan can promise a time.\n\nWeek 10 (RACE). N
 ot medical advice\; pain that changes how you move means stop.\nrampwise-
 plan
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
